  "body": "#2505: the kind check in `Tool::kind_rule` (`crates/tools/src/tool_sanity.rs`) ended with `_ => None`. A `ToolKind` added later passed the check with no kind rule. The equivalence test did not see it, because its kind list was written by hand.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/tools/src/tool_sanity.rs`: the `_ => None` arm is gone. The last arm names the 13 kinds that have no rule, or whose guarded rules held: `EndMill`, `BallNose`, `BullNose`, `Bore`, `Drill`, `Tap`, `Turning`, `Groove`, `Thread`, `Form`, `Taper`, `Probe` and `Torch`. A new `ToolKind` does not compile until this match names it.\n- `crates/tools/src/tool_sanity_tests.rs`:\n  - New `kind_slot`: an exhaustive match that gives each kind a slot. A new kind does not compile until it gets a slot.\n  - New test `the_sweep_list_holds_each_kind_once`: each slot occurs exactly one time in `KINDS`. A new slot fails the test until `KINDS` holds the new kind.\n  - The oracle `old_is_sane` keeps its `_ => true`. It is the old law, verbatim.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2505-exhaustive-kind-match.md`. It also says why there is no `ToolKind::ALL` constant: `tools.rs` has 691 lines.\n\n## Tests\n\n- A trial variant `ProbeKindForTest` added to `ToolKind` gives `E0004` at `tool_sanity.rs:108` (the kind rules) and at `tool_sanity_tests.rs:125` (`kind_slot`). The trial was removed.\n- `the_named_law_gives_the_old_verdict_everywhere`: green. Thus the verdicts for the 18 kinds do not change.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on d7aa843e5: green (tools lib; app `project_tool_refusal`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No behaviour changes, thus no UI or app suite other than the gate's selection was run.\n\nChangelog: none (no behaviour change)\n\nFixes #2505\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
